# Extension Injection Safety

When editing browser-extension integrations or remote Foldspace actions:

- Work one action at a time; split multi-action requests into separate discovery, plan, and build passes.
- Do not edit action code until the user has approved the implementation plan.
- Scope host permissions and CSP relaxations to the client sandbox domains only.
- Do not hardcode personal credentials, production customer credentials, bearer tokens, or session cookies.
- Treat action returns as LLM-facing. Return concise `{ success, message, data?, error? }` objects and strip stacks, tokens, internal URLs, and raw API errors.
- Validate params before calling customer APIs. Ask for user confirmation before irreversible or externally visible changes.
- Keep auth extraction centralized in `agent/utils.ts` or `agent/constants.ts` so reviewers can inspect it quickly.
- Reuse shared API helpers, styles, UI views, constants, and utilities instead of duplicating action-local code.
- Guard SDK and action bundle initialization against duplicate injection.
